{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfumTEPaCgNwMZydnaKqQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"In the installed `agents` package (0.27.0), the MCP client sends a `server/discover` request first. It uses the MCP v2 client and works out the protocol version for each connection, then picks one of two paths:\n\n- **Stateless servers** answer `server/discover`, and the client carries on from there.\n- **Older servers** (Legacy Streamable HTTP, SSE and RPC) don't answer it, so the client falls back to the classic `initialize` handshake on the same connection.\n\nOlder `agents` versions (before 0.20.0) opened with `initialize`. The package's own docs confirm this, in `node_modules/agents/docs/mcp-client.md:191`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":840,"cache_read_input_tokens":25700,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":840},"output_tokens":218,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d7bafd7e-ce0b-465f-8ea4-c583b417a85e","uuid":"767fe63e-ffd7-49cd-ab8f-81a6a79daff6","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:49:18.273Z","request_id":"req_011CfumTE8CMJC6bXXhVSkCn"}
